('alict_02007', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Data Creation ,................... , Removal of obsolete data', '["Data storing", "Data Management", "Data presenting", "Data gathering", "Data editing"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Data Management". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2007, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02008', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the primary difference between data and information?', '["Data is processed and information is raw and unprocessed", "Data is unprocessed raw information is data that has been processed and organized", "Data and information are synonymous and interchangeable", "Data refers to printed information refers to digital data", "Data is always information can only be text-based"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The primary difference between data and information lies in their state and usefulness. Data refers to unprocessed facts and which can be or in other formats. It is essentially the raw input by may not provide meaningful insights', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2008, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02009', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is true about information?', '["Information is valuable only if it is stored in physical archives for future reference", "Information remains static and does not require updates once it is created", "Information is useful without the need for context or interpretation", "Information and data are the and their utility is unaffected by their presentation format", "Information should be and relevant to be meaningful and useful"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "Information should be and relevant to be meaningful and useful". This follows from the standard definitions of data, information, and ICT processing concepts.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2009, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02010', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which statement about writable and rewritable optical discs is correct?', '["CD-R and allow multiple while Blu-ray discs do not. CD-R", "and can be rewritten up to a limited number of times", "Blu-ray discs do not support rewritable formats such as BD-RE. Blu-ray", "Writable discs store data in a pre -recorded while rewritable discs use a dye -based recording surface", "Rewritable discs are only compatible with older optical drives"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This is incorrect because CD-R (Recordable) and (Recordable) are write-once formats. Once data is it cannot be erased or overwritten. Blu -ray on the other ha have a rewritable format (BD-RE), which allows multiple rewrites', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2010, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02011', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following require(s) real-time processing?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "B and C only. B C"]'::jsonb, 4, '• Statement Monitoring and controlling the temperature of a nuclear reactor is a critical real-time system because any delay in response can lead to system or even catastrophic consequences', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2011, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02012', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A secret vault only opens if the correct code is entered. a thief tried entering letters instead but the system immediately rejected it. another thief left the input but the vault demanded an entry. a thief entered a five -digit but the system only accepted numbers between 1000 and 9999, so it was denied. ryia jydu th miqj" ysiaj ;enq wjidk myl 1000 9999 th is the correct order of validation methods used?', '["Presence check \u2192 Range check \u2192 Data type check", "Data type check \u2192 Range check \u2192 Presence check", "Data type check \u2192 Presence check \u2192 Range check", "Presence check \u2192 Data type check \u2192 Range check", "Range check \u2192 Presence check \u2192 Data type check mrdih \u2192"]'::jsonb, 3, '• Data Type Check Ensures that the input is of the correct type numbers instead of letters). Connection The first thief tried entering letters instead of but the vault rejected it immediately. • Presence Check Ensures that the input is not left empty', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2012, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02013', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following represents the correct sequence of steps in the data processing cycle?', '["Data gathering \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data", "Data validation \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data gathering \u2192 Data output \u2192 Data \u2192 \u2192", "Data gathering \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data output \u2192 Data", "Data processing \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data gathering \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data \u2192 \u2192", "Data gathering \u2192 Data storage \u2192 Data validation \u2192 Data processing \u2192 Data"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Sequence of steps in the data processing • Step Collecting necessary data and entering them into the computer. • Step Methods and techniques used to enter data accurately into the computer. • Step Data is converted to information according to the requirement of the user', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2013, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02014', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is a major advantage of DDR5 memory compared to DDR4?', '["DDR5 operates at lower frequencies than DDR4. DDR5\" DDR4 g wvq", "DDR5 has a lower data transfer rate than DDR4. DDR5", "DDR5 supports on-die error correction (ODECC). DDR5 on-die (ODECC)", "DDR5 has a lower voltage than DDR4 but higher power consumption. DDR5 DDR4 g wvq", "DDR5 is backward compatible with DDR4 slots"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. DDR5 starts at 4800 MT DDR5 4800 MT Option 2: DDR5 has a much higher transfer rate than DDR4 due to its architecture', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2014, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02015', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is the main function of secondary storage?', '["Execute programs", "Provide temporary memory", "Store data permanently", "Perform arithmetic operations", "Display information"]'::jsonb, 3, 'This question addresses the primary function of secondary storage in a computer system. Secondary storage refers to non-volatile storage meaning the data stored there remains intact even when the computer is powered off. m%Yakh', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2015, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02016', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What type of data storage medium does compact disk(CD) belong to?', '["Optical", "Solid State", "Magnetic", "Solid magnetic", "Thermal"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Option 1: Compact discs (CDs) use optical data storage. A laser reads and writes data by interpreting the presence or absence of tiny pits on the disc''s surface. Option 2: Solid-state storage utilizes flash memory similar to what you find in USB drives or SD cards', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2016, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02017', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'A check that ensures the data entered matches the expected such as entering numbers in a numeric is known', '["Range check", "Length check", "Type check", "Digit check", "Hash total"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Ensures data falls within a specific range age between 1 and 100). Option 2: Checks the number of characters in input phone number must be 10 digits)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2017, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02018', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'Which of the following is an example of a graphical user interface (GUI)?', '["Command Line Interface (CLI)", "Text-based menu", "Windows desktop environment", "Batch processing", "V oice recognition system"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Command Line Interface This is a text-based interface where users type commands to perform tasks. It''s not a GUI. Text-based menu fukqj While it involves some graphical elements like text and menu it''s still primarily text -based and not a full GUI', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2018, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
