('alict_02023', 1, 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', 'What is a key difference between structured and unstructured information?', '["Structured information is difficult to while unstructured information is easy to analyze", "Structured information has a predefined while unstructured information lacks a defined structure", "Unstructured information is stored in rows and while structured information is stored in random formats", "Structured information only includes text while unstructured information is multimedia only", "Unstructured information is always more reliable than structured information"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: False. Structured information is easier to analyze because it follows a predefined such as rows and columns. Unstructured like or is harder to analyze and often requires specialized tools. wmyiq Option 2: True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Introduction to ICT & Data/Information', NULL, 2023, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
