('alict_02188', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the most simplified form of A. (B + C) + A. (B + C) + A. B. C A. (B + C) + A. (B + C) + A. B. C', '["A. B. C", "A + B + C", "B + C", "A. (B + C)", "None of the lsisjla determine the correct ASCII value for \"CEDAB\", we need to convert each letter to its ASCII binary equivalent. \"CEDAB\" ASCII w.h tys ASCII iudk njg values for the letters"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A. B. C". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2188, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02189', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A programmer wants to send the word "HELLO" from one computer to another. The computers only understand so each letter is converted into a unique binary code before transmission. This system the programmer is using is', '["Unicode", "ASCII", "Binary Compression", "Hexadecimal", "Machine Learning"]'::jsonb, 5, 'To find the two''s complement of a binary we need to perform the following Convert the number to its one''s complement by flipping all the bits (0s become 1s and 1s become 0s). Add 1 to the one''s complement to obtain the two''s complement', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2189, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02190', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Answer 2''s complement of the value obtained when the following statement is trivialized?', '["001011112", "110101112", "010101012", "110101002", "001010112 Statement"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Grid computing is a set of computers working together to perform a specific task. lsysmhla The workload is divided among the computers and each computer has its own contribution toward the common goal. Its advantages are as follows. tys jdis • Process is quick', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2190, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02191', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following statements about binary conversion is correct?', '["Binary conversion changes a number into a base-16 system using only digits 0-9 and letters A-F", "Binary conversion represents numbers using only two typically 0 and 1, which computers can process", "Binary conversion is used to encrypt data for secure communication", "Binary conversion converts text directly into images for storage", "Binary conversion increases the decimal value of a number by multiplying it by 2"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Binary conversion represents numbers using only two typically 0 and 1, which computers can process". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2191, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02192', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What can be considered as data validation method', '["A only. A", "A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C", "A and D only. A D", "All of the What is the two''s complement representation of -79?"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A and C only. A C". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2192, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02193', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What octal number is equivalent to the decimal 0.3125?', '["1.248", "0.258", "0.248", "0.1258", "0.58"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "0.248". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2193, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02194', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is equals to -7610 + AC16 ?', '["1258", "101101112", "1408", "5916", "10610 Converting hexadecimal to 160 16 1 160+12 17210 Let''s convert this answer into other bases. fuu lr the correct answer is 1408. the correct answer number is 1408 3 Questions 4 and 5 are based on the below circuit"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "1258". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2194, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02195', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What will be the Q output if SET is turned to 0 ?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C Converting decimal to binary"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A only. A". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2195, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
