('alict_02204', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the Octal value equivalent to decimal 250.2510?', '["372.68", "372.28", "376.28", "376.48", "376.68 4. Steps of designing a digital circuit to solve a real world problem is given below. ienE Simplify equations using Karnaugh Maps"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Convert decimal 250 to Octal: 250(10) = 250(10) = 372(8). This matches "372.28".', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2204, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02205', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which coding system is most commonly used to encode text in different languages and includes characters from different scripts and symbols?', '["ASCII", "EBCDIC", "Unicode", "BCD", "Gray code"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Unicode". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2205, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02206', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following represents the bitwise XOR operation of the two binary foflys XOR lrkafka ljrla o? 10101110012, Answer is 00100000102 The bitwise XOR (exclusive OR) operation compares two bits and returns 1 if the bits are different and 0 if they are the same. To find the bitwise XOR of two binary we align them and perform the XOR operation on each corresponding XOR fufyhqu folla ixikaokh lr 1 iudk foll XOR fidhd wms XOR fufyhqu lrkafkuq'' Given Binary Numbers', '["110011102", "110010002", "101111012", "111111002", "101100102 The resulting binary number after performing the XOR operation is 0010000010. XOR fufyhqu"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "110011102". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2206, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02207', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'F516 - A0C16 = ...................? Answer : 5 ) Converting Hexadecimal to Binary 1 F 5 0001 1111 0101 00010001111101012 Converting Hexadecimal to Binary A 0 C 1010 0000 1100 1010000011002 Binary Subtraction 00010001111101012 - 1010000011002 = 0111111010012 Converting Binary to Hexadecimal 0111 1110 1001 7 E 9 7E916', '["E716", "E316", "D916", "F916", "E9"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "F916". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2207, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02208', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'If in what ASCII value is represented by the following signal?', '["F", "C", "G", "E", "I A = 65 B = 66 C = 67 D = 68 E = 69 F = 70 G = 71 H = 72 ASCII represents A as 65. ASCII u.ska A lrkqfha 65"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "F". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2208, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02209', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What does oct(10) return in oct(10) o@ Answer : 3 ) In the " oct() " function converts an integer to its octal representation as a string. The octal representation of a number is prefixed with "0o". Python tys string ioyd -0o- Wmi¾.h ioyka lr Answer', '["''10''", "''0o10''", "''0o12''", "''12''", "''0o1010'' 10"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "''10''". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2209, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02210', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', '100.7510 + 32.38 What is the value that suits the blank here? 100.7510 + 32.38 fuys w.h 74.210 B. 4A.616 C. 5) 3 2 .3 81 80 8-1 8 x 3 1 x 2 0.125 x 3 24 + 2 + 0.375 26.37510 26.37510 + 100.7510 = 127.12510 Octal value', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "None of the lsisjla 8 127 15 -7 1 -7 0 -1 .125 x 8 1.000 Hexa decimal value"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "A and B only. A B". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2210, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02211', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the 2''s complement of -810? -810 2 : 3) Let''s follow the calculations', '["100010002", "111110012", "111110002", "111110112", "1101110"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "100010002". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2211, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
