('alict_02213', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A. Machine language was used as the programming language in first generation During the first generation of Joseph Jacquard invented punch fcdaimaa Alan Turing is the father of Computer hkq John Mauchly and John Presper Eckert are the inventors of EDSAC. fcdaka fm%iam¾ EDSAC of the above is', '["True. In first-generation machine language was indeed used as the programming language. Machine language consists of binary represented by sequences of 0s and which directly correspond to the instructions that the computer''s central processing unit CPU can execute", "False. Joseph Jacquard did not invent punch cards. Herman Hollerith is credited with the invention of the first practical punched card system for tabulating and analyzing data", "True. Alan Turing is referred to as the \"father of computer science\" due to his groundbreaking work in the field of theoretical computer science and artificial intelligence", "False. John Mauchly and J. Presper Eckert are not the inventors of EDSAC. EDSAC (Electronic Delay Storage Automatic Calculator) was actually developed by Maurice fcdaka fm%iam\u00be EDSAC ixj\u00beOkh ,oafoa", "A and B only"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "True. In first-generation machine language was indeed used as the programming language. Machine language consists of binary represented by sequences of 0s and which directly correspond to the instructions that the computer''s central processing unit CPU can execute". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2213, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02214', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the result of subtracting 32.5 in octal from 522.25 in decimal ?', '["10000.102", "570.758", "495.62510", "570.258", "489.7510"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "495.62510". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2214, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02215', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', '(8416 - 100102) + (768 + 1010) = .................... Answer : 3 ) To solve this first we need to convert the above values to a same base. .Kkh', '["B16", "11100102", "BA16", "5516", "32110 Conversion of Hexa- decimal to binary"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "BA16". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2215, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02216', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'EBCDIC (Extended Binary Coded Decimal Interchange Code) This option is correct. EBCDIC uses 8 bits to represent each which allows for 256 possible characters. Compared to which typically uses 16 bits per EBCDIC would result in fewer bits for the same text file. Given that 7016 bits are used in and 22410 bits are used in Unicode for the same this comparison aligns with the difference in bit usage between the two coding systems. EBCDIC is the coding system x', '["BCD", "ASCII", "EBCDIC", "Gray code", "Data is insufficient"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "BCD". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2216, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02217', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which logic gate is commonly used as a building block for constructing arithmetic logic units (ALUs) wxl (ALU) lrkafka 3) In the Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) performs various arithmetic and logical operations. The design of an ALU involves a combination of different logic wxl (ALU) wxl ALU', '["1110011 BCD", "01110011 BCD", "11101010 BCD", "11100001 BCD", "011100112"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "1110011 BCD". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2217, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02218', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Converting the decimal part (0.75): fldgi', '["10011100.112", "10011101.012", "10011100.1012", "10011101.102", "10011100.1112 3"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "10011100.112". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2218, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02219', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Consider the following python = input (''Enter a Binary '') Decimal = int 2) print(Decimal) What is the output of the above python code when the user entered ''11110001'' as the input?', '["10", "101", "201", "241", "1010"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "241". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2219, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02220', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A communication system transmits 8-bit binary with each sequence representing a number in two''s complement format. If the transmitted sequence is 11110100, what is the equivalent decimal value?', '["-9", "-11", "-12", "11", "12"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "-12". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2220, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02221', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What will happen if you open a non-existent file in "r" mode?', '["It will create a new file. th kj f.dkqjla", "It will raise a FileNotFoundError. th FileNotFoundError tlla", "It will open the file in read-only mode. th wdldrfhka", "It will overwrite the existing file. th", "It will open the file in binary mode. th"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "It will raise a FileNotFoundError. th FileNotFoundError tlla". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2221, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02222', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following is a characteristic of analog computers?', '["Process binary data", "Process continuous data", "Utilize microprocessors", "Work with only discrete signals", "Use vacuum tubes"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Process binary data Analog computers do not process binary 1s) is the foundation of digital computing. this statement does not describe analog computers. 0 1 2) Process continuous data This is the defining characteristic of analog computers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2222, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02223', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'When the two binary numbers 101101002 + 010001112 are consider that the resulting number is a complement of the two and find its decimal value. 101101002 + 010001112 hk fol', '["5", "251", "-251", "-5", "4"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "5". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2223, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02224', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', '8910 + 1710 = ......... What is the binary value equivalent to the answer?', '["01101011", "01101010", "01100011", "01100010", "01111010"]'::jsonb, 2, '8910 + 1710 = 10610. fuys" 8910 + 1710 = 10610 Let''s convert addition of 89 and 17 which is 106 into binary. 106 89 17 Converting 10610 into Binary 10610 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 128 64 32 16 8 4 2 1 0 1 0 1 0 1 0 011010102', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2224, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02225', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What does UTF stand for in computing?', '["Universal Text Format", "Unicode Transformation Framework", "Unicode Transformation Format", "Unified Text Function", "Unified Transformation Format"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. Not a valid definition Option 2: Incorrect. UTF is a format not a framework UTF Option 3: Correct. UTF stands for Unicode Transformation which is a standardized method for encoding Unicode characters into binary data', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2225, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02226', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following is true about full adders compared to half adders?', '["Full adders do not consider carry input", "Half adders can add three binary bits at once", "Full adders produce both sum and carry outputs using two folla", "Full adders are simpler than half adders", "Half adders cannot handle carry from a previous fmr tk"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: This option is incorrect because full adders are specifically designed to handle three two significant bits and a carry-in from the previous stage. This makes them ideal for multi-bit binary addition. folla fmr isg Option 2: This option is incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2226, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02227', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Get the two''s complement of -3510', '["001010112", "111110102", "0010000002", "110010012", "100111112 Then the Two''s complement should be calculated by adding 1 to the one''s complement. bkamiq 1la foflys .Kkh complement of -3510"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Let''s simplify each option given in the question A) = A + BC + B ̅ + C̅ = A + C + B ̅ + C̅ Redundancy Law = A + B ̅ + C̅ + C Commutative Law = A + B ̅ + 1 Inverse Law = 1 Identity Law B) = X + XY + ZX + X ̅ = X + X ̅ + XY + ZX Commutative Law = 1 + XY + ZX Inverse Law = 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2227, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02228', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'A number is represented in three different bases as mdo flf¾( - (X)₁₆ = 100101110₂ - (X)₁₆ = (???)₈ If X is the hexadecimal equivalent of the binary what is its octal representation? X hkq iudk w.h tys : 1) Information and Communication ;dlaIKh 2026', '["456", "1236", "342", "235", "257"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Binary number We are told that this binary number is equivalent to X₁₆ in hexadecimal and we are to find its octal (base- 8) representation', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2228, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02229', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the decimal equivalent to the binary 101101.0012 g iudk 4) Explanation', '["45.5", "48.125", "65.5", "45.125", "50.25 Conversion of binary to 0 1 0 1 0 1 0 1 0 27 26 25 24 23 22 21 20 2-1 2-2-3 2-4 128 64 32 16 8 4 2 1 0.5 0.25 0.125 0.0625 32+8+4+1 = 45 0.125 45.12510 3. Simplify"]'::jsonb, 5, 'The expression X = AB + AB + AB can be simplified using the idempotent law of Boolean which states that X = AB + AB + AB In this the term AB is repeated three times. Applying the idempotent X = (AB) + (AB) + (AB) X = (AB) + (AB) X = AB', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2229, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02230', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Find the sign magnitude representation of -18 in an 8-bit 8ys -18 3) Explanation', '["00010010", "11100010", "10010010", "11001000", "101101"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Boolean Expression A Boolean expression is obtained and then simplified using Boolean laws. F = A + B. (BC + A. C) F = A + B + (BC + A. C) De morgan''s Law = (A+B)+(BC + A. C) Double complement Law = (A+B)+(BC)(A. C) De morgan''s Law = (A+B)+(B + C)(A', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2230, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02231', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'When the answer obtained from the calculation of 0.37510 + 0.87510 is converted into an octal the answer + 0.875 10 hk .Kkh ,efnk 1) Explanation', '["1.28", "1.38", "1.2510", "3.248", "1.1"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A Karnaugh map is a graphical method used to simplify Boolean expressions. By grouping the 1''s in the simplified Boolean expression can be derived. ldfkda', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2231, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02232', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which decimal value gives the 1''s complement of 100110012 represented by 8 bits?', '["-102", "102", "153", "-153", "103"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "-102". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2232, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02233', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'ASCII decimal representation for "A" is 65. "A" ASCII 65 of the following is true about representing "C" ? "C" The decimal ASCII representation 67', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and C only. A C", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Statement ASCII values increment by 1 for each subsequent uppercase letter in the English alphabet. bx.%Sis A = 65 B = 66 C = 67', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2233, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02234', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following functions is used to get the ASCII value of a character?', '["ord()", "chr()", "ascii()", "eval()", "hex()"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The function ord() is used in Python to obtain the ASCII value of a as correctly described in Option 1. When a character is passed to ord(), it returns the corresponding integer representation of that character in the ASCII table', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2234, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02235', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is the incorrect BCD value?', '["10011000", "01011001", "11001000", "10001000", "00110111"]'::jsonb, 3, 'BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) is a representation of decimal digits (0-9) using 4-bit binary numbers. Each 4-bit group in a BCD value must range from 0000 (decimal 0) to 1001 (decimal 9) to be valid. If any 4- bit group exceeds this the entire value becomes invalid', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2235, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02236', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'Which of the following ways checks whether the message traveled properly when carrying a message from one place to another? tla isg', '["Encryption", "Synchronization", "Parity Check", "Port scanning", "Modulation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Parity Check". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2236, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02237', 2, 'Number Systems & Data Representation', 'What is a qubit in quantum computing?', '["A classical binary bit that can be either 0 or 1. 0 1", "A unit of quantum information that can be 0, 1, or both simultaneously. 0\" 1\" folu", "A measure of computational speed in quantum computers", "A quantum error correction code", "A physical gate used to perform quantum operations"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "A unit of quantum information that can be 0, 1, or both simultaneously. 0" 1" folu". This follows from converting/calculating the given number(s) using standard place-value (base) arithmetic.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Number Systems & Data Representation', NULL, 2237, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02238', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the primary function of an operating system?', '["To provide an interface between hardware and software", "To permanently store user data", "To function as a programming language", "To only manage internet connections", "To execute only one program at a time"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To provide an interface between hardware and software An operating system (OS) is the main software that manages computer hardware and software resources. Its primary functions • Hardware Acts as an interface between hardware and applications', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2238, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02239', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Big data refers to extremely large and complex sets of information that are difficult to process using traditional methods. Which of the following isn''t a feature of Big Data?', '["Volume", "Veracity", "Velocity", "Versatility", "Variety"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Big Data is commonly defined by the 4Vs 1. V olume - Refers to the massive amount of data generated from different sources. - 2. Velocity - The speed at which data is and processed. - 3. Variety - Different types of data unstructured)', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2239, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02240', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements best describes a feedback loop in a system?', '["A process where the system resets itself after every operation. fufyhqulska miq", "A mechanism where the output is routed back to influence the input. wdodkhg", "A method to increase system speed by bypassing unnecessary logic", "A memory circuit that only stores values temporarily", "A data path that allows multiple inputs to be selected at once. nyq"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: This describes a reset not a feedback loop. Reset is a manual or triggered state not an ongoing output-input influence. fm%arl Option 2: This is the textbook definition of a feedback loop', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2240, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02241', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is NOT a file system j¾.hla fkdjkafka o? Answer : 4 ) Explanation', '["1", "A\u0305 + D\u0305 + B", "C + B\u0305 + D\u0305", "0", "B\u0305"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "1". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2241, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02242', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A disk with a FAT32 file system has clusters. Each cluster is 16 KB. How much data can this disk hold? FAT32 clusters cluster tllau 16 KB .; yels 3) Explanation', '["A + D", "C. B\u0305", "B. D", "1", "D"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A + D". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2242, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02243', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements is a key feature of an application software?', '["All these have to be paid for", "This type of software is relatively less used in the world", "User cannot use these more easily than system software", "A programming language", "Installing an operating system in computer system is more easy than installing application software"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "A programming language". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2243, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02244', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which is a wrong expression regarding quantitative data?', '["Quantitative data can be represented in an order", "Numbers are used to represent quantitative data", "Graphs can be used to process and represent quantitative data", "Shape and colour are quantitative data. yevh", "division can be done"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Quantitative data consists of numerical values that can be measured and expressed with allowing for mathematical operations like and division', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2244, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02245', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is correct about Grid computing ?', '["Grid computing is a set of computers that working together to perform a specific task", "Its process is quick. tys", "Has ability to process large quantities of data by decentralizing data", "Has ability to operate a single software from various locations", "All are correct"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Grid computing is a set of computers that working together to perform a specific task". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2245, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02246', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which type of computer is the least accurate in processing data such as speed used to process continuous data?', '["Digital Computer", "Analog Computer", "Micro Computer", "Hybrid Computer", "Computer"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Analog Computer". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2246, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02247', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A user is running a memory-intensive application while multitasking between other and then saves the edited file to the hard drive. Consider the following statements regarding the operating system features used in this Odjkh udre miqj ilia - Virtual memory allows the large application to execute by using secondary storage when physical memory is Odjkh - Context switching is responsible for saving and organizing the file structure on the hard drive. f.dkqj iq', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and C only. A C", "B and C only. B C", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "A only. A". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2247, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02248', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What was the significance of the ENIAC (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer), developed in the mid-1940s?', '["It was the first general-purpose electronic digital computer. th", "It was the first computer to use transistors instead of vacuum tubes", "It was the first computer to incorporate artificial intelligence. th", "It was the first computer to be connected to the internet. th", "It was the first computer to introduce the concept of virtual memory. th"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "It was the first general-purpose electronic digital computer. th". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2248, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02249', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is incorrect about issues caused by IT?', '["Protecting sensitive information from unauthorized users is known as the copyright. wkjir", "Phishing is gaining sensitive information of a person for mischievous deeds by misleading the owner", "Piracy is unauthorized duplication and distribution of copyrighted content by a third party. fidrlu", "Plagiarism is the process of taking someone''s ideas pretending that they are your own", "All are correct"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Followings are some issues caused by Information Technology. Confidentiality - Protecting sensitive information from unauthorized users is known as confidentiality. - wkjir ex : Passwords : Credit Stealing misleading the owner', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2249, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02250', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statement best describes an interpreted language?', '["An interpreted language is a programming language that is directly executed by the operating system without the need for compilation", "An interpreted language is a programming language in which the code is translated into machine code before execution", "An interpreted language is a programming language that is executed line -by-line by an interpreter at runtime", "An interpreted language is a programming language that must be compiled into bytecode before it can be executed", "An interpreted language is a programming language used exclusively for scripting web pages"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "An interpreted language is a programming language that is executed line -by-line by an interpreter at runtime". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2250, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, unit, unit_title, question_text, options, correct_option, explanation, latex_formula, trap_insight, difficulty, topic, past_paper_year, past_paper_number, series)
VALUES
('alict_02251', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In terms of relational database the cardinality ratio is a crucial concept that', '["The quantity of foreign key references established across the connecting related tables", "The total number of records or tuples contained within particular reflecting the size of dataset", "The maximal number of entities from one set that can be associated with entities from another set within a specific relationship", "The total count of attributes defined within an entity determining its schema structure. tys", "The execution order in which relational database management systems process and resolve relationships during query evaluation"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: Incorrect. While foreign keys are used to establish relationships between they are not the same as the cardinality ratio', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2251, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02252', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following best describes the process of ER to Relational Database Mapping?', '["Ensures that each primary key in the relational schema has a unique corresponding entity in the ER diagram", "Converts relationships and attributes in the ER model into a single flat table format. ER", "Transforms and attributes into relations while preserving constraints like primary keys and foreign keys", "Maps all entities directly into stored procedures and ignores relationships", "Focuses solely on normalizing attributes without considering relationships or keys"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This statement is partially true but does not fully capture the mapping process. While it is important that primary keys correspond to unique this statement does not encompass the broader aspects of how entities and relationships are transformed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2252, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02253', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the extension of the word CMOS?', '["Computational Matrix Optimization Service", "Creative Memory Organization System", "Complementary Metal-Oxide-Semiconductor", "Cryptographic Memory Overlay System", "Chronological Memory Operating System"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Complementary Metal-Oxide-Semiconductor". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2253, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02254', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which database model stores data in a single table without any relationships between records?', '["Relational model", "Hierarchical model", "Flat file system", "Network model", "Object-relational model"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The flat file system stores data in a single table without any relationships between records. In this data is organized in a tabular structure where all information is stored in rows and typically within a single like a spreadsheet', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2254, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02255', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the purpose of the fetch-execute cycle in computer architecture?', '["To fetch data from memory", "To execute instructions sequentially", "To process input", "To manage interrupts", "To handle exception handling"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "To execute instructions sequentially". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2255, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02256', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'If an entity in an ER diagram has a multivalued how is this attribute mapped into a relational schema?', '["The multivalued attribute is directly included as a column in the table representing the entity. nyq w.h", "A separate table is created for the multivalued with a foreign key referencing the primary key of the entity. nyq w.h", "The multivalued attribute is stored as a composite key in the table of the entity. nyq w.h", "The multivalued attribute is ignored during the mapping process", "The multivalued attribute is converted into a derived attribute in the relational schema. nyq w.h"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Option 1: Incorrect. A multivalued attribute cannot be stored in a single column as it can have multiple values for a single entity instance. nyq Option 2: Correct', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2256, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02257', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is incorrect about various computer types?', '["Super computers does parallel processing", "Mainframe computers are mainly made to handle huge number of output and storage data at once. m%Odk", "Mainframe purpose computers are also known as dedicated computers", "Analog computers are used to process continuous data", "Digital computers are used to process discrete data"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Mainframe purpose computers are also known as dedicated computers". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2257, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02258', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the output of the following Python = {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3} result = v**2 for v in data.items() if v % 2 == 1} print(result) Answer : 5) Let''s consider the process of this python code step by step. fuu mshjfrka = {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3} A dictionary named data is created with three key-value dictionary tlla hq., lr has the value 1', '["[''a'': 1, ''c'': 9]", "{''a'', ''c''}", "{1, 9}", "{1: ''a'', 9: ''c''}", "{''a'': 1, ''c'': 9} For each key-value pair where v is the comprehension creates an entry in result where the key is k and the value is v**2 (the square of v). v"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "[''a'': 1, ''c'': 9]". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2258, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02259', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which database model is best suited for supporting complex data structures and relationships?', '["Flat file system", "Hierarchical model", "Network model", "Relational model", "Object-relational model"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: The flat file system stores data in a tabular format like CSV files. It does not support relationships or complex data making it unsuitable for handling intricate data models. Option 2: This model organizes data in a tree-like structure with parent-child relationships', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2259, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02260', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements is correct regarding flowcharts?', '["Flowcharts can only represent linear processes", "Flowcharts are strictly for representing algorithms", "Flowcharts provide a visual representation of processes", "Flowcharts are limited to programming languages only", "None of the"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The correct statement is that flowcharts provide a visual representation of processes. Flowcharts are diagrams that illustrate the steps of a process or system. They use symbols like and arrows to show the flow of making it easier to understand complex processes', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2260, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02261', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which database model allows multiple relationships between forming a graph structure?', '["Flat file system", "Hierarchical model", "Relational model", "Network model", "Object-relational model"]'::jsonb, 4, 'The correct answer is 4) Network model. The network database model allows multiple relationships between records by representing data as nodes (records) and edges (relationships), forming a graph -like structure', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2261, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02262', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'In a what is denormalization?', '["The process of dividing a table into multiple smaller tables. j.=", "The process of merging tables into one table. j.= tl", "The process of adding more indexes to speed up queries", "The process of converting a normalized schema into a less normalized one for optimization", "The process of creating new foreign key constraints between tables. j.="]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: Incorrect. This describes not denormalization. Option 2: Incorrect. Although denormalization may involve combining it is done for performance not just merging. This option is too simplistic. Option 3: Incorrect', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2262, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02263', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'The type of operating system used for second generation computers ioyd j¾.h jkafka" Answer :3) Second-generation which were developed in the 1950s and primarily used single -user operating systems. These early computers were mainly batch processing meaning they processed jobs one at a time. The operating systems of that era were not as advanced as later generations and supported only a single user at a time without multitasking or multi-user capabilities. 1950 1960 .Kka ixj¾Okh ,o fojk m%Odk thska woyia tlska tl', '["Multi-user nyq", "Multi-threading nyq which allows multiple threads to execute is a feature of modern operating not second-generation systems. nyq", "Multi-tasking nyq", "Multi-programming nyq where several programs are loaded into memory and executed started in the later part of the third generation. lsysmhla", "Multi user nyq"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "Multi-user nyq". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2263, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02264', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements about compiler and assembler is false?', '["Both produce an output that can be directly processed by the computer. folu", "Both detects errors before execution. folu", "Both are essential in the software development process", "Assembler Operates at a high level and compiler Operates at a low level", "Assembler has minimal optimization capabilities and compiler has often includes various optimization techniques"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Assembler Operates at a high level and compiler Operates at a low level". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2264, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02265', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is NOT considered a file 4) Explanation', '["File name ku", "File location", "Owner", "File system", "File size"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "File name ku". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2265, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02266', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the logical view of a file in computing?', '["How the file is stored on secondary storage", "How the operating system sees the file", "How users or programmers see the file", "How the file is transferred over a network", "How the file is backed up"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is the physical not the logical view. Option 2: This refers to the system''s internal view of file management. 1) B̅ + CA 2) C̅ + BA 3) C + B̅A 4) B + CA̅ 5) C + B̅A̅ A. C B̅ Option 3: This is the correct description of the logical view', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2266, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02267', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'A student is using a computer to write a report. They have their word processing program open and they save their report to a USB drive when they are finished. YsIHfhla Tjqka Tjqkaf.a jpk jevigyk th wjika miq Tjqka ;u USB Odjlhlg iqrlshs'' Which operating system feature is most directly involved when the student saves their report to the USB drive?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'When the student saves their report to the USB the operating system''s file system management features are directly responsible for handling this action', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2267, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02268', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the value of output after the following code is miq output w.h fldmuKo? def = 0 for i in i % 2 == += -= i return result output = tricky_loop(5) Answer : 2) Explanation', '["0", "2", "4", "10", "The given Python code defines a function tricky_loop(n) that iterates over the range of n and alternates between adding and subtracting the loop variable i to the result based on whether i is even or odd. When the function is called with n = 5, the loop processes values from 0 to 4. It adds even numbers (0, 2,"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "0". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2268, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02269', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the main role of the system call interface in an operating system?', '["To provide an interface for user applications to interact with the hardware", "To manage network connections", "To allocate memory to processes", "To handle file system operations", "To provide an interface for user applications to request services from the kernel"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Option 1: User applications don''t interact directly with system call interface provides an intermediary layer to request services rather than directly managing hardware', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2269, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02270', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following steps is NOT typically involved in the process of collecting data from an HTML form and inserting that data into a database? HTML fmdaruhlska', '["Retrieving the data from the form using PHP. PHP", "Sending the data to the server using an request", "Parsing and validating the data on the server side. fiajdodhl", "Directly updating the database schema without modifying the table structure. j.=", "Inserting the validated data into the database using a server-side script (Ex. Node.js). fiajdodhl"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Correct answer: "Directly updating the database schema without modifying the table structure. j.=". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2270, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02271', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is a key characteristic of an agile development approach?', '["Strict adherence to initial requirements", "Sequential and linear development process", "Flexibility and iterative development", "Long development cycles", "Limited user involvement"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "Flexibility and iterative development". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2271, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02272', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the primary purpose of an expert system?', '["To process large amounts of data quickly", "To automate repetitive tasks", "To simulate human decision-making abilities", "To store vast amounts of information", "To control hardware devices"]'::jsonb, 3, 'An expert system is a type of computer program designed to mimic the decision -making abilities of a human expert in a specific field. Let''s evaluate the given options Option 1: Incorrect. The expert systems might analyze but their main purpose is not rapid data processing', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2272, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
