('alict_02274', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'What is the primary goal of Business Process Reengineering (BPR)?', '["To automate existing business processes", "To incrementally improve processes over time", "To reduce costs by outsourcing business activities", "To fundamentally redesign business processes for dramatic improvements", "To focus only on enhancing customer service operations fiajd"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Business Process Reengineering (BPR) is about making drastic changes to existing aiming for significant improvements in performance measures such as and speed', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2274, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02275', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Q = ((A + B). A) Which of the following circuits implement this lrkafka 1) Explanation', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C", "All of the 4. A system uses a 32-bit virtual address and has a page size of 4 KB. Each page table entry (PTE) takes 4 bytes. What is the size of the page table for a single process?"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A 32-bit virtual address means the process can access 232 bytes (or 4 GB) of virtual memory', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2275, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02276', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'You are managing a project using the Waterfall where each phase of development must be completed before the next one begins. Midway through the development your client requests significant changes to the system requirements. How should you handle this situation according to the principles of the Waterfall model?', '["Immediately stop the current implement the and continue from where you left off", "Complete the current document the change and then start the entire process again from the feasibility study phase", "Ignore the changes until the system is fully then make the changes during the maintenance phase", "Incorporate the changes during the testing phase to minimize disruption to the development process", "Allow the client to make minor adjustments during the current phase and continue without restarting the process"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Complete the current document the change and then start the entire process again from the feasibility study phase". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2276, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02277', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Enterprise Resource Planning Systems (ERPS) typically', '["Only financial operations", "Manufacturing and inventory management", "Only HR and payroll systems", "All core business processes like and supply chain management", "Social media and marketing functions"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Enterprise Resource Planning Systems (ERPS) are designed to integrate and streamline all the key functions within an organization. They create a centralized system that connects various allowing data to be easily shared and accessible across the organization', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2277, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02278', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following statements best describes the repetitive waterfall model in', '["It emphasizes continuous feedback and iterative development without predefined phases. th", "It allows for revisiting previous phases to refine and improve the software based on feedback", "It strictly follows a linear progression through the phases without any backtracking. th", "It is suitable only for small projects with minimal complexity. th", "It does not involve documentation at any stage of the development process"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In the repetitive waterfall the development process is divided into distinct such as requirements and similar to the traditional waterfall model', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2278, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02279', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following best describes the concept of "feedback" in a system?', '["The initial input provided to the system", "The final output produced by the system", "Information about the system''s output that is returned to the input or control mechanism to influence future operations", "The process of converting raw data into meaningful information. raw", "The internal components and structure of the system"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Feedback is a fundamental concept in systems theory where information about a system''s output is routed back to its input. tys This mechanism allows the system to self -regulate and adapt its future behavior based on its past performance', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2279, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02280', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following best describes bio-inspired computing?', '["Computing systems that only use biological materials", "Algorithms and systems designed based on biological processes and organisms", "Traditional computing methods without any biological references", "Computing that focuses solely on human biology. udkj", "Use of living organisms to perform computations. .Kkh"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "Algorithms and systems designed based on biological processes and organisms". This reflects standard operating-system concepts (process/file/memory management) as usually taught at A/L.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2280, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02281', 5, 'Operating Systems & File Management', 'Which of the following is not a component of a context diagram?', '["The system represented as a single process", "External entities that interact with the system", "Data flows showing information moving between the system and external entities", "Detailed internal processes of the system", "Inputs and outputs exchanged with external entities"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A context diagram shows the system as a single its interactions with external and the data flows (inputs and outputs) between them. It does not show detailed internal th', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Operating Systems & File Management', NULL, 2281, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
