('alict_02300', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is a valid variable name in kduhla 2) Explanation', '["1variable", "variable_1", "variable-1", "variable!", "@variable In variable names must start with a letter or an underscore ( _ ) and can only contain and underscores. Special characters like ''-'', ''!'' and ''@'' are not and variable names cannot start with a number. the valid variable name is variable_1 , as it starts with a letter and includes an which is allowed. The other options are invalid because they either start with a number or contain special characters that are not permitted in Python variable names. Python"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "variable_1". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2300, 'A/L Past Paper Series')
