('alict_02336', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following best describes the difference between mutable and immutable data types in Python?', '["Mutable objects can be", "Immutable objects can be modified in", "Mutable objects can be changed after", "Only strings are", "Mutable and immutable objects behave the same in memory"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In mutable objects (like and sets) can be changed after they are created. For you can add or remove elements in a list', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2336, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
