('alict_02338', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about Python is not true?', '["Python is a high-level programming language", "Python is case-sensitive", "Python code must be compiled before it runs. Python", "Python can be used for web development", "Python supports object-oriented programming. Python"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Option 1: This is true. Python uses English-like syntax and is designed to be easy for humans to read and write. Option 2: This is true. For a variable named Variable is different from variable. Option 3: Python is an interpreted not a compiled one', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2338, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
