('alict_02377', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is the correct way of implementing the if condition in python?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "A and B only. A B", "A and C only. A C"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "C only. C". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2377, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02378', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about the Python range() function is correct?', '["step) can generate a decreasing sequence only if step is positive. step) Ok", "The stop value in range() is always included in the generated sequence. range()", "Using a negative step in range() allows you to generate a sequence in reverse order. range() mshjrla", "range(5) generates the sequence [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]. range(5) [1, 2, 3, 4,", "The range() function can only be used inside for loops. range()"]'::jsonb, 3, 'step) Generates a sequence of numbers. Negative step Allows counting backwards (reverse order). wdmiq .Kka bv fohs Option 1) A positive step cannot generate a decreasing Option 2) The stop value is excluded in range sequences', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2378, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
