('alict_02381', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'a = b = c = 2, 5.5, ''python'' Which statement is correct related the above Python statement?', '["All three variables c have the same data type. c hk", "This is a syntax error statement. syntax", "All three variable names are tuple. c hk", "The three variable names are and string data types. c hk", "All three variable names have the same value. c hk"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In the statement a = b = c = 2, 5.5, assigns the same value to all three variables and c. The right-hand side is a tuple (2, 5.5, ''python''), which means Python does not assign 2 to 5.5 to and to c. the entire tuple is assigned to each of them', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2381, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
