('alict_02383', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What would be the output of the following Python = price + (price * tax) - (price * discount) return total print(calculate_total(100)) print(calculate_total(100, 3) Explanation', '["A + BC\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305\u0305", "A + BC", "A\u0305 + B\u0305C", "A + BC\u0305", "A\u0305(B\u0305 + C)"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Correct answer: "A̅ + B̅C". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2383, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02384', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'How can you convert a list into a set in Python?', '["set(list_name)", "list_to_set(list_name)", "convert_set(list_name)", "set_list(list_name)", "set_of(list_name)"]'::jsonb, 1, '1) set(list_name) This is the correct way to convert a list into a set in Python. The set() function takes an iterable (like a list) as an argument and returns a set with unique elements. For set([1, 2, 2, 3]) will produce {1, 2, 3}', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2384, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02385', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following is used to get the below output?', '["print(x , sep = ''a'')", "x.join(''a'')", "x.join(a)", "''a''.join(x)", "join = ''a'')"]'::jsonb, 4, 'To get the above output we should use the join method the correct way to use the join method is given in the answer 4), we cannot use the print function to change a string because strings are we can only change a copy of the string not the actual string itself. Answer is 4) 9', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2385, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02386', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following Python code(s) would compile without generating an error?', '["A only. A", "B only. B", "C only. C", "B and C only. B C", "A and C only. A C Tuples are immutable in meaning you cannot modify them. The pop() method is used to remove elements from not tuples. This will raise an error"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Correct answer: "A and C only. A C Tuples are immutable in meaning you cannot modify them. The pop() method is used to remove elements from not tuples. This will raise an error". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2386, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
