('alict_02414', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What built-in Python function will return the length of a string? String tll ,nd fokafka 1) Explanation of the answers', '["len() This is the correct answer. The len() function in Python returns the number of items (length) of an object. For it returns the number of characters", "str() This is incorrect. The str() function converts an object to its string representation. It does not return the length of a string. str()", "size() This is incorrect. There is no built-in size() function in Python that returns the length of a string. Python", "length() This is incorrect. There is no built -in length() function in Python. The correct function for this purpose is len(). Python built-in length()", "sizeof() This is incorrect. The sizeof() function is not a built -in function in Python for strings. In other programming such as sizeof is used to determine the size of a data type or object in but it is not used to get the length of a string in Python. sizeof() function tl strings"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "len() This is the correct answer. The len() function in Python returns the number of items (length) of an object. For it returns the number of characters". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2414, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
