('alict_02417', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statement about while loops in Python is true?', '["A while loop will always execute at least regardless of the condition. while", "The condition in a while loop is evaluated before each iteration", "A while loop can only be used to iterate over lists. while", "You can only use break statements inside a for not a while loop. Tng", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Correct answer: "The condition in a while loop is evaluated before each iteration". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2417, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
