('alict_02419', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the following Python n == n + func(n - 1) print(func(4)) Which of the following statements about this code is true?', '["The function func(n) calculates the sum of all integers from n to 1 and returns the result. func(n)", "The function func(n) will return the value 4 when called with the argument 4. func(n)", "The base case of the recursion is n == 0, so the function will return 0 when n is 0", "The function func(n) will return 15 when called with the argument 4. func(n)", "The function func(n) will work correctly if n is less than 1. func(n)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Correct answer: "The function func(n) calculates the sum of all integers from n to 1 and returns the result. func(n)". Trace through the code line by line (variable assignments, loop iterations, and function calls) to confirm this result.', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2419, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
