('alict_02464', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the following modified Bubble Sort ,o Bubble Sort = len(arr) for i in = False for j in range(0, n - i - arr[j] > arr[j + arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j] swapped = True if not arr What is the purpose of the swapped variable?', '["To keep track of the largest element in each pass. mdia", "To ensure the function sorts only the first half of the array", "To terminate the loop early if the array is already sorted", "To identify the smallest element in the array", "To reduce the time complexity"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Outer Loop This loop ensures that all elements are though the swapped condition may break it early if the array becomes sorted before completing all passes. fmr Inner Loop Compares adjacent elements (arr[j] and arr[j + 1]) and swaps them if they are in the wrong order', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2464, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02465', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is the main difference between a list and a tuple in Python?', '["Lists are while tuples are mutable", "Lists are while tuples are immutable", "Lists can only store while tuples can store any type of data", "There is no difference between lists and tuples list tuple tlla", "None of the above"]'::jsonb, 2, 'In the main difference between lists and tuples lies in their Python tuples m%Odk fjki Lists • Mutable. Their contents can be changed after creation. • You can or modify elements in a list. Tng Tuples • Immutable', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2465, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02466', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following Python functions will close an open file?', '["f.close()", "f.stop()", "f.end()", "close(f)", "f.end_file()"]'::jsonb, 1, 'To close an open file in use the close() which is called on the file object after done using it. Python f = open("example.txt", "r") f.close() Why the other options are incorrect 2) f.stop() Incorrect because stop() is not a valid file object method in Python. stop() 3) f', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2466, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02467', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What is the purpose of the is operator in Python?', '["To check equality of two values", "To compare the memory addresses of two objects", "To check if a variable exists", "To perform logical operations", "To test for membership in a list"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The operator in Python is primarily used to compare the memory addresses of two as described in Option 2. It checks whether two variables reference the same object in rather than simply comparing their values', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2467, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
