('alict_02474', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about dictionaries is false?', '["A dictionary can contain other dictionaries as values. dictionary tll", "Dictionary keys must be immutable objects. dictionary", "Dictionary values can be of any data type. dictionary", "Dictionary keys are case-insensitive by default. dictionary", "Dictionaries are iterable in Python. dictionary"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Option 1: This is true. A dictionary can contain other dictionaries as values. This is often referred to as a nested dictionary. dictionary tll Option 2: This is true', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2474, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02475', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following methods is used to read a single line from a text file in Python?', '["readline()", "readlines()", "read()", "readfile()", "readtext()"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The readline() method in Python is used to read a single line from a text file. It reads characters from the file until it encounters a newline character with open("example.txt", "r") as line = file.readline() print(line) readlines(): Reads all lines from the file and returns them as a list', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2475, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
