('alict_02477', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'How do you insert an element at the beginning of a list in Python?', '["list.insert(0, element)", "list.append(element)", "list.add(0, element)", "list[0] = element", "None above"]'::jsonb, 1, '1) list.insert(0, element) The insert() method in Python is used to add an element at a specific position in a list. The syntax list.insert(0, element) inserts the given element at index 0, which is the beginning of the list. Python insert() iskagelaia list.insert(0, element) 2) list', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2477, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02478', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'How do you fetch all rows from a query result using Python''s database cursor object?', '["cursor.fetchall()", "cursor.get_all()", "cursor.fetch()", "cursor.all()", "cursor.retrieve()"]'::jsonb, 1, '• cursor.fetchall() Correct. This method retrieves all rows of a query result and returns them as a list of tuples. It fetches the entire result set at once. th • cursor.get_all() Incorrect. This is not a valid method for fetching rows', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2478, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02479', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following Python data types allows modification of its elements after creation?', '["Strings", "Tuples", "Lists", "None of the above", "All of the above"]'::jsonb, 3, 'In a List is a mutable data which means its elements can be changed after creation (you can or modify items). Python Strings and Tuples are immutable (cannot be modified after creation). Strings Tuples the only correct option is Lists', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2479, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02480', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'What does the pop () method do when called on a Python list?', '["Removes the first element from the list", "Adds an element to the end of the list", "Retrieves and removes the last element from the list", "Reverses the order of elements in the list", "Sorts the list in descending order"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The pop() method in Python is used to remove and return the last element of a list by default. Here''s how it Python pop() th fukak( Example numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50] removed_element = numbers', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2480, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02481', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements about the help() function in Python is true?', '["help() is used to exit the Python interpreter", "help() can only be used on built-in not user-defined functions. help()", "help() provides documentation about Python and objects. help() u.ska", "It can be used only on not on modules or classes. th", "It modifies the function or object it is used on. th"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Statement False. help() is not used to exit the Python interpreter. exit() or quit() is used for that. quit() Statement False. help() can be used on both built-in and user-defined as well as modules and objects. Statement True', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2481, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
('alict_02482', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Consider the below python = [32, 45, 51, 60, 74, 85, 91] for score in score % 5 == will be the output?', '["32 51 74 91", "32 45 51 60 74 85 91", "32 51 60 74 85", "45 60 85", "Error"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The list scores contains the [32, 45, 51, 60, 74, 85, 91]. scores A for loop iterates through each score in the list. for The if statement checks whether the score is a multiple of 5 (score % 5 == 0). if 5 oehs 1', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2482, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
