('alict_02490', 6, 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', 'Which of the following statements best describes the difference between a function and a method in Python?', '["Functions are defined using the def while methods are not", "Methods can be called without any whereas functions always require arguments. lsis\u00f7 argument tllska", "Functions are standalone blocks of while methods are functions that belong to an object", "Methods can return whereas functions cannot. Methods ,nd yels", "Functions are used for mathematical while methods are used for string operations"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The statement that best describes the difference between a function and a method in Python is "Functions are standalone blocks of while methods are functions that belong to an object', NULL, NULL, 'medium', 'Programming Concepts (Python/PHP)', NULL, 2490, 'A/L Past Paper Series'),
